1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:10,950
Dan, please buy four carrots, three tomatoes, and one cucumber. The blue list is for my salad.

2
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:26,550
And six potatoes, two onions, and some broccoli for my soup. Two lists, Dan. Please keep them separate.

3
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:36,200
Blue is salad. You have it?

4
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:41,950
Blue salad, yellow soup. I have it.

5
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:51,200
Should we check those together?

6
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:56,950
No need. I have an excellent memory.

7
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:03,750
Blue soup, yellow salad. Easy!

8
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:11,850
Dad, that is already backward. Maybe your pocket needs a better filing system.

9
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:20,550
We can help. I will check the vegetables.

10
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:28,050
And I will carry the basket. Does broccoli need a seat belt?

11
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:36,200
Ready, team?

12
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:41,950
Ready. Even the empty basket looks hungry.

13
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:55,950
Welcome to the market, team. We need vegetables, not surprises. Stay together, and let's check every item.

14
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:06,750
Can you carry the basket, Dad? It is very heavy.

15
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:09,450
But it is empty!

16
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:12,750
I am saving my muscles for later.

17
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:21,200
The vegetable stand is on the right.

18
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:26,950
Right. My first useful direction today.

19
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:36,200
Our basket has the blue handle.

20
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:41,950
Good. We are not shopping for someone else.

21
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:47,550
Forty carrots, please.

22
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:50,250
Four, Dad. Four carrots.

23
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:55,950
Good catch. Forty would need their own shopping cart.

24
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:04,350
One, two, three, four. Four carrots.

25
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:10,650
Exactly. I was just checking whether you were paying attention.

26
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:21,200
Four feels much lighter than forty.

27
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:26,950
And much easier to carry home.

28
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:36,150
We need three tomatoes. These are red and ripe.

29
00:03:36,450 --> 00:03:38,850
Three little bowling balls?

30
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:43,350
Only if you want tomato soup everywhere.

31
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:52,350
One tomato, three tomatoes. I have the words and the numbers.

32
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:56,850
Great. Now keep the tomatoes round, please.

33
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:06,200
They are tomatoes, not bowling balls.

34
00:04:06,550 --> 00:04:11,950
Then I promise no strikes today.

35
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:20,550
A cucumber! Long, green, and ready for salad.

36
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:28,050
That is a zucchini, Dad. The cucumber is in the next crate.

37
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:35,550
This is a cucumber. That is a zucchini.

38
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:41,850
Two green cousins. I should have checked their names first.

39
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:51,200
These two look similar, but they are different.

40
00:04:51,550 --> 00:04:56,950
I will remember the bumps.

41
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:06,200
Dad, the yellow list is still hiding.

42
00:05:06,550 --> 00:05:11,950
Then we should give it some fresh air.

43
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:21,150
Six potatoes for the salad. That sounds very crunchy.

44
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:27,450
Maybe we should check which list belongs to which dish.

45
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:34,950
How many potatoes do we need? Six.

46
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:43,650
Six potatoes. I can count them. I just cannot decide where they are going.

47
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:51,200
Potato salad? That was not the plan.

48
00:05:51,550 --> 00:05:56,950
Maybe the lists are telling different stories.

49
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:04,950
These onions are making me cry already.

50
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:12,450
You have not cut them, Dad. Maybe they heard your potato-salad plan.

51
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:21,150
One onion, two onions. Which bag do they need?

52
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:28,050
An excellent question. Let us keep the evidence together for now.

53
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:36,200
No tears. The onions are innocent.

54
00:06:36,550 --> 00:06:41,950
Then we close the case for now.

55
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:52,950
Look! A tiny tree. Can we plant a forest in the basket?

56
00:06:53,250 --> 00:06:58,050
It is broccoli, Max. A very tasty-looking forest.

57
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:04,950
We need some broccoli for Nina's soup.

58
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:08,850
Then the forest is going swimming.

59
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:12,750
Finally, one vegetable knows its destination.

60
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:21,200
Does our little forest need sunlight?

61
00:07:21,550 --> 00:07:26,950
Not for the ride home.

62
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:36,200
The red peppers are next.

63
00:07:36,550 --> 00:07:41,950
Great. I can hear success coming.

64
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:50,550
A bell pepper. I cannot hear the bell.

65
00:07:50,850 --> 00:07:57,450
It is named for its shape, Dad. It does not ring.

66
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:06,750
Maya wants one red bell pepper, not a green one.

67
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:13,050
Red pepper, silent bell. I am learning so much today.

68
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:21,200
No ringing. Just a very good pepper.

69
00:08:21,550 --> 00:08:26,950
And the correct color, finally.

70
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:34,350
We need two ears of corn.

71
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:38,250
Ears? Can the corn hear us?

72
00:08:38,550 --> 00:08:43,350
Only if you tell a very corny joke.

73
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:49,950
Two ears of corn for the soup.

74
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:55,650
Please do not tell the onions about the forest.

75
00:08:55,950 --> 00:08:58,950
Our shopping has secrets now.

76
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:06,200
What if the corn tells us a secret?

77
00:09:06,550 --> 00:09:11,950
Then we will keep it hushed.

78
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:20,550
This lettuce looks like a green bowling ball.

79
00:09:20,850 --> 00:09:27,450
That one is cabbage. We need the loose-leaf lettuce beside it.

80
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:34,350
This lettuce has loose, curly leaves.

81
00:09:34,650 --> 00:09:38,850
So do I on a windy morning.

82
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:43,350
Your hair is not on either list.

83
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:51,200
My hair looks like lettuce today.

84
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:56,950
Only when the wind helps.

85
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:06,200
I think we have one thing left.

86
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:11,950
Excellent. My basket agrees.

87
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:21,150
One bag of spinach. That is the last item.

88
00:10:21,450 --> 00:10:28,050
Wonderful. My basket is full, and my memory is almost full.

89
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:34,950
Wait. Blue says salad. Yellow says soup.

90
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:41,850
Your vegetables are correct. Your two dinner plans have changed places.

91
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:51,200
The groceries are right. The dinner names are wrong.

92
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:56,950
We can fix the bags before we leave.

93
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:04,350
How is my salad coming along?

94
00:11:04,650 --> 00:11:07,050
Six potatoes and broccoli.

95
00:11:07,350 --> 00:11:13,350
That sounds like Nina's soup wearing a salad name tag.

96
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:18,750
Could you repeat that, please?

97
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:26,250
We need salad and soup, not an argument between potatoes and tomatoes.

98
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:36,200
Read the colors slowly, Dan.

99
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:41,950
Blue salad. Yellow soup. Message received.

100
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:51,200
You do not have to remember everything.

101
00:11:51,550 --> 00:11:56,950
Then I should ask more questions.

102
00:12:00,750 --> 00:12:07,350
I mixed up the lists. I wanted to get everything right.

103
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:14,250
You can make a mistake and still be a good dad.

104
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:22,950
We are a team. Let us read one list at a time.

105
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:28,650
And no vegetable has to argue with another vegetable.

106
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:36,200
Thank you for helping me fix this.

107
00:12:36,550 --> 00:12:41,950
We can do it. One vegetable at a time.

108
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:52,350
Maya's salad: carrots, tomatoes, cucumber, lettuce, and a red bell pepper.

109
00:12:52,650 --> 00:12:56,250
Blue list, blue bag. Everything matches.

110
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:05,550
Nina's soup: potatoes, onions, broccoli, corn, and spinach.

111
00:13:05,850 --> 00:13:11,850
Yellow list, yellow bag. The forest found its swimming pool!

112
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:21,200
Two bags, two dishes. Correct at last.

113
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:26,950
And no one has to eat potato salad soup.

114
00:13:30,750 --> 00:13:33,150
How much is everything?

115
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:36,450
Eighteen dollars and fifty cents.

116
00:13:36,750 --> 00:13:41,550
Good. The teamwork was free, but extremely valuable.

117
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:49,950
We have twenty dollars. That is enough.

118
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:57,450
Here you go. One twenty. I checked the number twice this time.

119
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:06,200
A good meal is worth careful shopping.

120
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:11,950
And a careful receipt check.

121
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:20,550
Your change is one dollar and fifty cents.

122
00:14:20,850 --> 00:14:24,450
Change? Do we need new clothes?

123
00:14:24,750 --> 00:14:28,350
This change is money coming back.

124
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:34,950
Twenty minus eighteen fifty is one fifty.

125
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:43,050
The receipt is right, the bags are right, and I am finally right.

126
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:51,200
My shirt stays green. The money comes back.

127
00:14:51,550 --> 00:14:56,950
Exactly. Two meanings, one good joke.

128
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:06,200
Blue for Maya. Yellow for Nina. Everybody ready?

129
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:11,950
All three kids. All ten ingredients.

130
00:15:15,750 --> 00:15:21,750
Maya, here are your salad vegetables. Blue list, blue bag.

131
00:15:22,050 --> 00:15:28,050
Perfect. And you remembered to bring our children home, too?

132
00:15:30,750 --> 00:15:33,750
All three children. We counted.

133
00:15:34,050 --> 00:15:40,050
And my soup vegetables! Did the broccoli enjoy its trip?

134
00:15:40,350 --> 00:15:43,950
It asked for a window seat.

135
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:51,200
You brought exactly what we needed.

136
00:15:51,550 --> 00:15:56,950
And you brought a funny story with it.

137
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:06,750
First, wash your hands. Then we will wash the vegetables.

138
00:16:07,050 --> 00:16:08,850
Even the cucumber?

139
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:11,550
Especially our well-traveled cucumber.

140
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:21,150
Wash the cucumber. Put it on the clean plate.

141
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:25,050
Exactly. You are giving clear instructions.

142
00:16:25,350 --> 00:16:28,350
My cucumber understands English now.

143
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:36,200
I will do the cutting.

144
00:16:36,550 --> 00:16:41,950
Then I will set the napkins.

145
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:48,150
Shopping finished. Dinner finished!

146
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:55,650
You brought the ingredients, Dan. They have not learned to cook themselves.

147
00:16:55,950 --> 00:16:58,950
That is tomorrow's English lesson.

148
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:06,750
First, we prepare the vegetables. Then we make the salad.

149
00:17:07,050 --> 00:17:13,050
And I cook the soup. Two dishes, one happy kitchen.

150
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:21,200
Six plates. One for each of us.

151
00:17:21,550 --> 00:17:26,950
Dinner really is coming together.

152
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:36,200
The salad is ready.

153
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:41,950
And so is the soup. Everyone, take a seat.

154
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:51,150
I felt embarrassed because I mixed up the lists.

155
00:17:51,450 --> 00:17:58,650
We helped because we love you. You help us learn every day.

156
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:04,950
You listened, asked questions, and tried again.

157
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:11,850
That is a good recipe for learning. Even without forty carrots.

158
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:21,200
Would forty carrots need forty chairs?

159
00:18:21,550 --> 00:18:26,950
Only if they came to dinner as guests.

160
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:33,750
If you are unsure, ask.

161
00:18:34,050 --> 00:18:38,850
And if a vegetable has ears, speak politely.

162
00:18:39,150 --> 00:18:42,150
That second rule is optional.

163
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:53,550
I will ask when I am unsure. Could you check this with me?

164
00:18:53,850 --> 00:18:59,250
Of course. Asking for help is always welcome here.

165
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:06,200
We can keep the lists where everyone sees them.

166
00:19:06,550 --> 00:19:11,950
Next time, I will check before I guess.

167
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:19,950
Tomorrow, we need fruit for a picnic.

168
00:19:20,250 --> 00:19:22,050
One list, please.

169
00:19:22,350 --> 00:19:24,750
One list. Two colors.

170
00:19:25,050 --> 00:19:27,450
And three excellent helpers.

171
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:43,350
Today we brought home vegetables, new words, and a better plan. One family, one team. See you at the fruit shop!

172
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:51,200
Tomorrow, we can choose fruit together.

173
00:19:51,550 --> 00:19:56,950
I like that plan. Especially the together part.

